          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Deb"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Just made these, they are delicious! The cookie I was looking for a tad crunchy but soft inside. They came out so pretty and puffed and uniform. I did use 1 TBS. white sugar and 1 TBS. brown sugar mixed with the cinnamon to roll them in. Also lightly sprinkle this mix over them as soon as I moved parchment off cookie sheet. Had to make a 2nd batch of cinnamon sugar to coat the 56 cookies I got. Enough left for cinnamon toast.",
            "datePublished": "2023-12-20T03:50:21.588Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Eliza"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I've made this recipe at least a dozen times, everyone loves them. I ended up changing up 2 things. I adjusted the cook temp to 365° instead of 400° because I kept getting flat and crunchy cookies; the cook time is the same. Make sure you remove them from the cookie sheet immediately after taking them out of the oven. I also adjusted the coating to be 3TBS white sugar and 3tsp cinnamon for a better flavor",
            "datePublished": "2021-04-27T22:31:56.420Z"
          },
          {
